From 3c47f847e7f07a1f3037f76665987713adcc960b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michiel <367462+meghuizen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:33:59 +0200
Subject: [RFC PATCH net-next 2/4] net/sched: sch_cake: use a Weyl sequence for
 the quantum dither

cake_get_flow_quantum() adds get_random_u16() to
flow_quantum * quantum_div[host_load] before the shift, so that the
rounding does not accumulate in one direction.  It runs at every DRR
deficit refill and when a flow becomes active, under the qdisc lock.
With n bulk flows behind one host the quantum is about flow_quantum / n,
so a packet of length L costs about L * n / flow_quantum refills.

The dither has to be spread uniformly over [0, 65535], not be
unpredictable.  An additive sequence with an odd step visits every
16-bit value once per 65536 steps.  Keep one per tin and step it by
0x9e37 instead of calling get_random_u16().  The u16 goes into the hole
after flow_quantum, which cake_get_flow_quantum() reads anyway, so
struct cake_tin_data does not grow (pahole).

Not measured: neither the cost of get_random_u16() on this path nor the
resulting change.

Tested: sch_cake.o builds without warnings (W=1) on x86_64.

Assisted-by: Claude pahole
---
Impact: low -- CAKE with many bulk flows behind one host.  Not
demonstrated: no measurement of get_random_u16() on this path.

- One sequence is shared by all flows of a tin, so with n flows served
  in turn each flow sees every n-th value.  For n a power of two that is
  a fixed residue class, which biases the dither by at most n/65536 of
  a byte per refill.

 net/sched/sch_cake.c | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/sched/sch_cake.c b/net/sched/sch_cake.c
index a8836a30b9e6..88a9a843c037 100644
--- a/net/sched/sch_cake.c
+++ b/net/sched/sch_cake.c
@@ -155,6 +155,7 @@ struct cake_tin_data {
 	u16	overflow_idx[CAKE_QUEUES];
 	struct cake_host hosts[CAKE_QUEUES]; /* for triple isolation */
 	u16	flow_quantum;
+	u16	quantum_dither;	/* see cake_get_flow_quantum() */
 
 	struct cobalt_params cparams;
 	u32	drop_overlimit;
@@ -700,11 +701,14 @@ static u16 cake_get_flow_quantum(struct cake_tin_data *q,
 		host_load = max(host_load,
 				q->hosts[flow->dsthost].dsthost_bulk_flow_count);
 
-	/* The get_random_u16() is a way to apply dithering to avoid
-	 * accumulating roundoff errors
+	/* Dither to avoid accumulating roundoff errors.  An additive
+	 * (Weyl) sequence spreads the dither uniformly over [0, 65535],
+	 * which is all the correction needs.
 	 */
+	q->quantum_dither += 0x9e37U;
+
 	return (q->flow_quantum * quantum_div[host_load] +
-		get_random_u16()) >> 16;
+		q->quantum_dither) >> 16;
 }
 
 static u32 cake_hash(struct cake_tin_data *q, const struct sk_buff *skb,
